              "question": "<p>Which enzyme catalyses the committed, rate-limiting step of de novo purine synthesis?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>PRPP synthetase</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>PRPP synthetase activates ribose-5-phosphate to PRPP, the substrate for the committed step, but it is not the rate-limiting enzyme of the de novo pathway itself.</div>",
