                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Glutamine-PRPP amidotransferase</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. This enzyme catalyses the committed step, converting PRPP to phosphoribosylamine. It is activated by PRPP and inhibited by the end products AMP, GMP, and IMP.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>HGPRT is the key enzyme of the salvage pathway, not the de novo pathway. It recycles free purine bases using PRPP.</div>",
